# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent scratch — never committable.
#
# 2026-08-31: two files sat untracked-but-NOT-ignored in this PUBLIC repo,
# each carrying a hardcoded GitHub token on line 1:
#
#   .claude/check-flatsbo-prs.mjs   const TOKEN = 'ghs_…'   (mtime 2026-07-19)
#   output-file                     a bare ghs_…            (mtime 2026-08-02)
#
# `git check-ignore` returned nothing for either, and `.claude/` is a TRACKED
# directory — so a single `git add -A` would have published a GitHub
# credential to a public repository. Both were `ghs_` App-installation tokens
# with a ~1h TTL and both were already expired when found (probed against
# api.github.com: HTTP 401, twice). The credential was dead. The MECHANISM
# was live, and the mechanism is what these rules close.
#
# For whoever edits this next: deny by default in the places agents write,
# then re-admit named exceptions. A list of the two filenames that leaked is
# not a control — the next agent will pick a different name.

# `.claude/` cannot be ignored wholesale: `.claude/agents/` holds reviewed,
# committed config. So deny the directory's contents and re-admit only that.
# Everything else an agent drops there — scratch .mjs, scraped JSON, launch
# configs, token dumps — is ignored from here on. This supersedes the older
# `.claude/worktrees/` line, which it fully covers.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/

# Ad-hoc output sinks: an agent invents a filename, redirects a secret into
# it, and never cleans up. `output-file` was exactly this shape. Every rule
# here is root-anchored so the tracked `outputs/` tree stays tracked.
/output-file
/output-file.*
/out
/out.*
/tmp-*
/.tmp-*

# Root-level dot-prefixed agent scripts and probes. `.get-token.mjs` — which
# mints a fleet token — and `.mk-pr.mjs` are live examples on disk today, and
# neither was ignored before this change. Real root dotfiles (.gitignore,
# .eslintrc.json, .env.example) carry other extensions and are unaffected.
/.*.mjs
/.*.cjs
/.*probe*

# Secret-shaped filenames anywhere in the tree.
*.token
token.txt
tokens.txt
*-token.txt
*_token.txt
*.credentials
credentials.json

# A blessed place for scratch, so nobody has to invent a root-level filename.
/.agent-scratch/

# prisma generated
/prisma/generated/

# Sentry — never commit auth tokens or wizard-generated rc files.
# `.sentryclirc` is generated by `npx @sentry/wizard` and contains an
# auth token; `.env.sentry-build-plugin` is the alternate plugin-format.
# See docs/runtime-alerting-2026-05-18.md.
.sentryclirc
.env.sentry-build-plugin

# Fleet automation tokens — short-lived GitHub tokens minted by the fleet
# push/PR mechanism. NEVER commit. Live only on local disk; in-memory preferred.
.fleet-token*.txt
.fleet-token*.err
*.fleet-token.txt
*.fleet-token.err
.night-*.mjs
.night-*.md
.mk-junction*.mjs
.pr-body*.md
pr-sweep.mjs
*.private-key*
.playwright-mcp/

# Playwright E2E artifacts
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
